<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Otto I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">crowned <a href="/years/962">962 CE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Otto I of Saxony</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-the-illustrious">Otto I, Duke of Saxony</a> and King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, was crowned emperor by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-john-xii">Pope John XII</a> in 962 CE. He had earlier defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magyars">Magyars</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-lechfeld">Battle of Lechfeld</a> in 955. His coronation is the date most historians treat as the functional founding of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/otto-i.jpg" alt="Otto I" width="320" height="310" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Otto Posse · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Siegel_Otto_I_Posse.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
